<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">1954 Guatemalan coup d'état</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1954</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Operation PBSuccess</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The 1954 Guatemalan coup d'état overthrew the elected president <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jacobo-arbenz">Jacobo Árbenz</a>, whose land reform had expropriated unused land of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-fruit-company">United Fruit Company</a>. Organised by the CIA under the code name Operation PBSuccess, it combined an invasion from Honduras by a small force under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carlos-castillo-armas">Carlos Castillo Armas</a> with propaganda and air raids; the army refused to fight, and Árbenz resigned on 27 June 1954. Decades of military rule followed.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/1954-guatemalan-coup-detat.jpg" alt="1954 Guatemalan coup d'état" width="320" height="252" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:President_Eisenhower_and_John_Foster_Dulles_in_1956.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
